<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:s="https://wvusports.com/services/xml_schema/story" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title /><link>https://wvusports.com/rss/</link><description /><atom:link href="https://wvusports.com/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><language>en-us</language><ttl>60</ttl><item><title>Mountaineers Defeat Coastal Carolina for Fourth Consecutive Victory</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/mens-soccer-mountaineers-defeat-coastal-carolina-for-fourth-consecutive-victory</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/mens-soccer-mountaineers-defeat-coastal-carolina-for-fourth-consecutive-victory</guid><category>Men's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Julen Recalde celebrates after scoring a goal against Coastal Carolina" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/29/msoc_vs_coastal-4.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.VA. (Oct. 29, 2026) – The No. 13 West Virginia University men's soccer team picked up its fourth straight victory with a 2-0 win over Coastal Carolina, Thursday evening at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium. The Mountaineers improve to 9-2-4 and 5-1-2 in the Sun Belt while the Chanticleers fall to 5-6-4 and 3-3-2 in conference play.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/msoc_vs_coastal-4.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/msoc_vs_coastal-4.jpg"><media:title>Julen Recalde celebrates after scoring a goal against Coastal Carolina</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/msoc_vs_coastal-4.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:45:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59613</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Roll Frostburg State in Thursday Night Exhibition</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/womens-basketball-mountaineers-roll-frostburg-state-in-thursday-night-exhibition</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/womens-basketball-mountaineers-roll-frostburg-state-in-thursday-night-exhibition</guid><category>Women's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Divine Tumba drive for a layup in the Mountaineers exhibition win over Frostburg State on Thursday, Oct. 29 inside Hope Coliseum" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/29/WBBALL_vFrostburg_102926-13.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – West Virginia rolled in its only preseason game of the season, downing Frostburg State 111-41 on Thursday night at Hope Coliseum.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/WBBALL_vFrostburg_102926-13.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/WBBALL_vFrostburg_102926-13.jpg"><media:title>Divine Tumba drive for a layup in the Mountaineers exhibition win over Frostburg State on Thursday, Oct. 29 inside Hope Coliseum</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/WBBALL_vFrostburg_102926-13.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:36:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>9</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59612</s:story_id></item><item><title>Hellmann Named Big 12 Men's Diver of the Week</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/mens-swimming-diving-hellmann-named-big-12-mens-diver-of-the-week</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/mens-swimming-diving-hellmann-named-big-12-mens-diver-of-the-week</guid><category>Men's Swimming &amp; Diving</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Levi Hellmann has been named the Big 12 Men's Diver of the Week for the week of Oct. 29, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/29/Swim26_Big12Awards_1920x1080_hellmann.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Junior Levi Hellmann of the West Virginia University men's swimming and diving team has been named Big 12 Men's Diver of the Week by the Big 12 Conference.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/Swim26_Big12Awards_1920x1080_hellmann.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/Swim26_Big12Awards_1920x1080_hellmann.jpg"><media:title>Levi Hellmann has been named the Big 12 Men's Diver of the Week for the week of Oct. 29, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/Swim26_Big12Awards_1920x1080_hellmann.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>7</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59610</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Take on Iowa State on First Stop of Road Swing</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/volleyball-mountaineers-take-on-iowa-state-on-first-stop-of-road-swing</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/volleyball-mountaineers-take-on-iowa-state-on-first-stop-of-road-swing</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WVU Volleyball team huddles before a point against Arizona" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/29/DAK01986.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University volleyball team (11-8, 4-5 Big 12) travels to Ames, Iowa, to take on Iowa State at Hilton Coliseum. First serve is set for 7:30 p.m. ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/DAK01986.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/DAK01986.jpg"><media:title>WVU Volleyball team huddles before a point against Arizona</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/DAK01986.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:52:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59611</s:story_id></item><item><title>WVU Olympic Sports Coaches Show Lineup For November</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/general-wvu-olympic-sports-coaches-show-lineup-for-november</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/general-wvu-olympic-sports-coaches-show-lineup-for-november</guid><category>General, Men's Swimming &amp; Diving, Rifle, Women's Swimming &amp; Diving, Wrestling</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="The WVU Olympic Sports Coaches Show will have three episodes in November 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/29/2026-27_Olympic_Sport_Coaches_Show-Nov.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The Mountaineer Sports Network from Learfield has announced the November schedule for its popular WVU Olympic Sports Coaches Show live from the Mountain State Brewing Company in Morgantown.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/2026-27_Olympic_Sport_Coaches_Show-Nov.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/2026-27_Olympic_Sport_Coaches_Show-Nov.jpg"><media:title>The WVU Olympic Sports Coaches Show will have three episodes in November 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/2026-27_Olympic_Sport_Coaches_Show-Nov.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:30:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>3</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59607</s:story_id></item><item><title>Forbes Named to Katrina McClain Award Watch List</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/womens-basketball-forbes-named-to-katrina-mcclain-award-watch-list</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/womens-basketball-forbes-named-to-katrina-mcclain-award-watch-list</guid><category>Women's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Skylar Forbes takes part in a preseason practice ahead of the 2026-27 season" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/29/GB706710.jpg" /><br /><br />SPRINGFIELD, MASS. — The Naismith Basketball Hall of Fame announced the 20 watch-list candidates for the 2027 Karl Malone Award and, in partnership with the Women's Basketball Coaches Association (WBCA), the 20 watch-list candidates for the 2027 Katrina McClain Award. The annual Karl Malone Award, named after the Class of 2010 Hall of Famer and two-time NBA Most Valuable Player, celebrates its 13th year by recognizing the top power forward in NCAA Division I men's college basketball. The Katrina McClain Award, now in its 10th year, recognizes the top power forward in NCAA Division I women's college basketball. It is named after the two-time All-American, 1987 National Player of the Year, and Class of 2012 Hall of Famer.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/GB706710.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/GB706710.jpg"><media:title>Skylar Forbes takes part in a preseason practice ahead of the 2026-27 season</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/GB706710.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>9</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59605</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Set to Close Fall Season at D1 Invitational</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/tennis-mountaineers-set-to-close-fall-season-at-d1-invitational</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/29/tennis-mountaineers-set-to-close-fall-season-at-d1-invitational</guid><category>Tennis</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Rio Maeda returns a serve at the 2026 Wahoowa Invitational" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/29/IMG_9182.jpeg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University tennis team travels to Rome, Ga., for the D1 Invitational from Oct. 29-Nov. 1 at the Rome Tennis Center at Berry College.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/IMG_9182.jpeg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/IMG_9182.jpeg"><media:title>Rio Maeda returns a serve at the 2026 Wahoowa Invitational</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/29/IMG_9182.jpeg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>T